Scope and third-party material

The MIT License above covers the code in code/ and reproduce/, and the data we
created: datasets/RQ2 (framework snippets), datasets/RQ4 (bug-fix pairs), the
ClassEval mutants, the behavior-preserving rewrites, and everything in results/.

Third-party material keeps its original license:
  datasets/RQ5/humanevalpack/   HumanEvalPack (Muennighoff et al.), MIT License
  datasets/RQ5/classeval/       ClassEval (Du et al.), MIT License
  datasets/family_clustering/   corpus released by Yun et al. (FSE 2026)
  datasets/RQ3/                 problem list from neetcode-gh/leetcode (MIT
                                License); solutions and complexity labels from
                                the public NeetCode solution pages, included for
                                research use only
Model weights are not redistributed. They are downloaded from Hugging Face under
their own licenses when the embedding scripts run.
